// SOLID Principles
// S: Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) : A class should have only one reason to change, it should do only one thing and not multiple responsibilities.
// O: Open-Close Principle (OCP) : A class should be open for extention but closed for modification. We must not change the old code to add new feature.
// L: Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP) : Subclasses should be subsitutable for their base classes.
// I: Interface Segregation Principle (ISP) : Many client specific interfaces are better than one general purpose interface. The client should not be forced to implement the methods they don't need.
// D: Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP) : High Level module should not depend on the low level module, but rather both should depend on the interface module.
